{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeRMRRB3CzKEDy25nTDXM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The defect is in `codec/encode.go`, in `FieldOrder()`:\n\n```go\nfunc FieldOrder() string { return \"name,id,active\" }\n```\n\nThis returns fields in the wrong order — `\"name,id,active\"` — whereas the declared struct/field order expected by the test (and presumably by the golden data format) is `\"id,name,active\"`. Since `id` should come first (matching declaration order) but `name` and `id` are swapped, `TestDeclaredOrder` fails.\n\n**Root cause:** `FieldOrder()` hardcodes/returns fields out of their declared order (name before id), rather than reflecting the actual declaration order `id, name, active`. This is a source bug in the encoder's field-ordering logic (likely it iterates/sorts fields incorrectly, or the hardcoded string was mistyped), not an issue with the test or the golden.json data.\n\nFix would be changing the returned order to `\"id,name,active\"` in `encode.go` — no changes to `testdata/golden.json` needed, confirming the defect is isolated to `FieldOrder()`'s implementation in `codec/encode.go`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":233,"cache_read_input_tokens":2302,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":233},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"654602e6-11eb-40a5-9a37-cd1cf66a36e9","uuid":"620e9a03-b7e4-4d02-92ed-be2cbf78bc66","timestamp":"2026-08-26T12:23:04.811Z","request_id":"req_011CeRMRQJT31JMDrWsryGjB"}
